{"duration_api_ms":36985,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"9df243c5-858b-4a9f-a49d-f3650abde083","total_cost_usd":0.0434519,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":36113,"output_tokens":1662,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1357},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":9,"output_tokens":1662,"cache_read_input_tokens":36113,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":7591,"outputTokens":14,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.007660999999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-4-5":{"inputTokens":9,"outputTokens":1662,"cacheReadInputTokens":36113,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0357909,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":1357,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Looking through the provided material:\n\n## 1. What guarantee does the API make about an article's slug?\n\n**The slug is unique (enforced by the database schema) and auto-generated, serving as a stable identifier for retrieval, updates, and deletion.** The navigation map explicitly states \"Article.slug is unique\" in the Prisma schema, and the `SlugGenerator` handles \"slug generation and uniqueness.\"\n\n## 2. How does an article or profile response reflect the REQUESTING user's relationship to the author (following, favorited), including for anonymous/unauthenticated requests?\n\n**Article responses include a `favorited` boolean and the author object includes a `following` boolean; for unauthenticated requests, both default to `false`.** The tests show authenticated users see `favorited: true` after favoriting and `following: true` in profiles after following, while the profile test demonstrates unauthenticated GET returns `following: false`.\n\n## 3. What makes an incoming request authenticated, and what happens when the token is missing or invalid?\n\n**A request is authenticated via the `Authorization: Token <jwt-token>` header; missing or invalid tokens return HTTP 401 Unauthorized.** The tests consistently verify this pattern across all protected endpoints, and the navigation map confirms `AuthMiddleware` verifies the request token using `JwtTokenService`.","ttft_ms":31500,"type":"result","duration_ms":36011,"uuid":"9123e3ed-0441-45b2-96b8-b1299b1c587f","ttft_stream_ms":5193,"time_to_request_ms":31,"first_content_frame_ms":5523,"queued_turn_count":0}
